1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,560
Previously on JoJo's Bizarre Adventure!

2
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:07,560
Come out.

3
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:09,440
It's time to go home.

4
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:10,780
Ugh, get lost.

5
00:00:10,980 --> 00:00:12,860
I didn't ask you to come here.

6
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:15,320
You really think you can help me?

7
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:19,557
I'd like you to meet an Egyptian
friend I met a few years ago.

8
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:21,600
Say hello to Avdol.

9
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:31,320
Red Boy!

10
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:33,240
Huh? What the?

11
00:00:37,860 --> 00:00:39,340
And now for the truth.

12
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:42,934
This may seem like an evil
spirit, but it's far from it.

13
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:44,090
Jotaro,

14
00:00:44,173 --> 00:00:47,697
this thing you believe has possessed
you is actually a powerful vision,

15
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:49,780
created by your own life energy.

16
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:53,880
This vision will always
appear standing by your side.

17
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:57,100
And because of that, we call it a stand!

18
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:00,977
That coffin's a hundred years
old, and four years ago,

19
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:04,177
it was pulled out of the
Atlantic, off the coast of Africa.

20
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:05,160
Okay, so?

21
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:07,060
I did a little research.

22
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:12,180
My grandfather, Jonathan Joestar, your
great-grandfather, died while at sea.

23
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:17,060
Turns out this exact same coffin was
on that boat with him when he died.

24
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:20,817
When they discovered it four
years ago, it was empty,

25
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:23,917
but I know exactly what was inside it.

26
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,140
Avdol and I are trying to
locate him as we speak.

27
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:29,240
That person is evil incarnate!

28
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:31,160
And his name is Theo!

29
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:35,077
And now that he has been awakened
from his hundred-year slumber,

30
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:38,240
it is our fate to fight that man!

31
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:42,720
From the neck of this bastard
on down is Jonathan Joestar!

32
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,600
My grandfather!

33
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:47,194
This son of a bitch took over his body!

34
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:00,720
Jotaro, don't leave yet.

35
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,120
You forgot something important.

36
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:04,540
Silly boy.

37
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,240
Here is your goodbye kiss.

38
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:09,660
You're such a bitch.

39
00:02:10,060 --> 00:02:12,797
Stop clinging to me like
I'm still a little kid.

40
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:13,710
Okay.

41
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:15,440
Have a nice day.

42
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:21,120
What a giant pain in my ass.

43
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:31,340
Hey, look, it's Jojo! What? Jojo?

44
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:34,920
You're right, it is Jojo!
Jojo! Jojo! Hey, Jojo!

45
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:36,257
What's up, Jojo?

46
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:37,281
Hey there, Jojo!

47
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:38,390
What's going on, Jojo?

48
00:02:38,473 --> 00:02:39,897
So tell me, Jojo, where have you been?

49
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:42,392
You haven't been to school for four days!

50
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:44,850
Hey!

51
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:48,237
Who do you think you are,
grabbing off to Jojo like that?

52
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:50,057
I don't like how friendly
you're getting with him.

53
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:50,970
Stay away!

54
00:02:51,053 --> 00:02:51,883
What the hell, ugly?

55
00:02:51,966 --> 00:02:53,077
I'd be careful there.

56
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:53,990
No boobs.

57
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:55,550
Ugh!

58
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:09,020
Shut up!

59
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:10,671
You're freaking annoying!

60
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,037
Ahhhh he totally said that to me!

61
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,000
Ahhhh me?!

62
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:19,540
JoJo!

63
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:58,500
What the hell?

64
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:08,320
Those branches.

65
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:12,600
Jojo!

66
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:14,320
Oh, no! No!

67
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,402
JoJo fell so far down the steps!

68
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,912
Look, he can still move!

69
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:20,394
The branches must have broken his fall!

70
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:24,600
Did a branch slash open my leg?

71
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:26,460
No, wait a sec.

72
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:29,757
That's not what caused me
to fall down the stairs.

73
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:32,580
This cut is what came first. But how?

74
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:41,520
I see.

75
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:45,652
Hey, looks like he's able to
summon a pretty fierce stand.

76
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,420
I get it now.

77
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:50,930
Impressive.

78
00:04:51,013 --> 00:04:53,333
No wonder he wants me to get rid of him.

79
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:55,480
But still...

80
00:04:57,720 --> 00:05:00,620
He is no match for the power of my stand.

81
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,840
Let's go.

82
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:16,180
Take it out with the strong style of gold!

83
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:43,617
you'd have cracked your
head right on the flagstone.

84
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:46,137
Nasty accidents happen on
those steps all the time.

85
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:50,338
Tomorrow when you go down these
steps, you really should hold my hand.

86
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,060
Here, your leg seems to be cut.

87
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:09,697
You might want to wrap it with this
handkerchief to help stop the bleeding.

88
00:07:09,780 --> 00:07:10,777
You gonna be okay?

89
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:13,080
Yeah, I'm fine. It's just a scratch.

90
00:07:18,260 --> 00:07:19,140
Hold it!

91
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:21,490
Hmm?

92
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:25,260
I forgot to say thanks.

93
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:27,129
I haven't seen you before.

94
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,515
You go to our school?

95
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:30,640
I'm Noriyaki Kakyoin.

96
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:33,389
And yes, I just
transferred here yesterday.

97
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:34,800
See you around.

98
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:38,520
Oh! Oh! Oh!

99
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:43,280
Oh, so his name's Kakyoin.
Seems pretty cool. You think so?

100
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:45,517
I still like Jojo way more than him.

101
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:46,430
Yeah, me too.

102
00:07:46,513 --> 00:07:47,343
Same goes for me.

103
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:56,020
At that time, I was very weak.

104
00:07:57,880 --> 00:08:00,160
Lacking a body made me vulnerable.

105
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:07,880
If I had not taken
Jonathan Joestar's body...

106
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:12,760
If it hadn't been for his energy,

107
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:15,300
to augment my own limited source,

108
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:19,914
I couldn't have survived at the bottom
of that ocean for a hundred years.

109
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:25,060
But still, this body has like a
bond between a parent and a child.

110
00:08:26,140 --> 00:08:27,820
It ties me to his kin.

111
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:35,697
They seem to know of my existence,

112
00:08:35,780 --> 00:08:41,840
and of this power I've gained
from taking Jonathan's body.

113
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:44,420
The Stand.

114
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:50,040
It is the Stand that reaches out
to the bodies of his descendants.

115
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:55,140
There are always advantages and
disadvantages to every situation.

116
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:58,497
I will eliminate them all.

117
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:02,520
The Joestar clan must be destroyed soon.

118
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:11,860
Why is every single room in
this house so tiny and cramped?

119
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:17,520
This is exactly why I hate Japan Avdol,
how the hell can you stand being here?

120
00:09:17,820 --> 00:09:19,997
I find it quite fascinating.

121
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:22,177
Especially the tea ceremony.

122
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:23,997
Ceremony shmaramony.

123
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:26,021
Instant coffee will do just fine.

124
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,160
By the way, about Dio.

125
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,600
Mr. Joestar,

126
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,400
if you and I are aware of his existence,

127
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:44,740
would it not be safe to assume
that he knows about us as well?

128
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:47,790
Hmm.

129
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:50,520
But if we don't know
what he's going to do,

130
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:53,307
or for that matter, even
what powers he has,?

131
00:09:55,940 --> 00:09:58,240
Japanese coffee is absolutely vile!

132
00:09:58,740 --> 00:10:00,160
That's American coffee.

133
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:05,220
That's a horrible cut, Jojo.

134
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:06,360
How'd you get it?

135
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:09,417
Let me guess, you got into
another fight, didn't you?

136
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:11,777
Show some respect and take off that hat.

137
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:12,960
It's poor manners.

138
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,740
Would you stop that? Seriously?

139
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:18,611
Has Jojo ever been hurt in a fight before?

140
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:20,397
That's not what caught him, I'm sure.

141
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:21,310
No way!

142
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:23,849
Well, you do have a point.

143
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:28,576
Then I'll assume you were
being clumsy, you big klutz.

144
00:10:28,980 --> 00:10:29,920
Hey, hold on.

145
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,297
What are you gonna do?

146
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:32,909
Cut your pants, of course.

147
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:34,380
Like hell you are.

148
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:36,857
Well, if I'm gonna treat
that wound, I must.

149
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:37,770
You ruin him.

150
00:10:37,853 --> 00:10:38,839
I'll take him off.

151
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:41,662
Didn't know you were so thrifty.

152
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:42,710
So,

153
00:10:42,793 --> 00:10:44,537
while JoJo's taking off his pants,

154
00:10:44,620 --> 00:10:48,217
I'm gonna take your temperatures and prove
you're nothing but a bunch of fakers.

155
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:49,997
Come on, we really caught a cold.

156
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:50,910
Totally.

157
00:10:50,993 --> 00:10:52,737
Now just let us go home already.

158
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:54,620
Not gonna happen.

159
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:57,650
Oops.

160
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,540
What the hell is this?

161
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:06,850
Kakyoin.

162
00:11:06,933 --> 00:11:07,763
Hey, Doctor!

163
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:10,820
What are you trying to do?

164
00:11:14,780 --> 00:11:16,280
What does it look like?

165
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:19,680
I'm just shaking out the
thermometer to reset it!

166
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:24,597
Th-that's not a thermometer
you got in your hand!

167
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:26,140
Yeah, that's a pen!

168
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:27,280
Oh, come on!

169
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:28,755
Did you just say pen?

170
00:11:28,900 --> 00:11:30,018
You think I'm dumb?

171
00:11:30,140 --> 00:11:33,000
Does this look like a pen to you?!

172
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:35,420
Tell me something!

173
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:38,780
Just how stupid are you two boys?!

174
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:44,637
If you honestly think this thermometer
I'm holding looks like a pen to you...

175
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:50,940
Then maybe you need to take a closer look!

176
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:04,550
What the?

177
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:17,570
Ah!

178
00:12:17,653 --> 00:12:18,483
My eyes!

179
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:19,580
My eyes!

180
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:24,720
JoJo, what do you have to say?

181
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:29,900
You're not gonna stand there and tell me
this thermometer looks like a pen too,

182
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:30,950
are you?

183
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,620
What the hell is going on?

184
00:12:37,740 --> 00:12:39,916
Such strength, this is no mere woman.

185
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:44,275
Wait, I saw something weird
crawling up from the floor.

186
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:46,397
Was it a stand?

187
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:47,780
Noriyaki Kakyoi.

188
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:49,897
Was he the one who started this?

189
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:51,917
Did he cut my leg on the stone steps?

190
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,460
Yes, it was me.

191
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:55,820
So it is you.

192
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,657
Hey, long time no see.

193
00:12:58,740 --> 00:13:02,900
So my stand is currently possessing
and controlling that doctor.

194
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:09,360
If you attack my stand,
you'll hurt her too, Jojo.

195
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:11,300
You bastard.

196
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:12,717
Who are you?

197
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:18,940
I told you, I'm Noriyaki Kakyoin, and the
name of my stand here is Hierophant Green.

198
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:22,940
I am human, but I have
pledged loyalty to him.

199
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:26,020
That's why I'm gonna kill you.

200
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:47,120
I have zero intention of hurting her.

201
00:13:48,980 --> 00:13:52,360
Now that I've dragged it
out, I see it for what it is.

202
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:56,220
Just a sleazy stand whose only
ability is to possess people.

203
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:04,120
So this is your stand? Kakyoin?

204
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:07,440
This green stripy thing
looks like a shiny melon.

205
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:10,720
You're gonna regret doing that.

206
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:14,020
Dragging that out of
her was a mistake, Jojo.

207
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:16,940
Don't act tough.

208
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:19,909
I can see my finger
marks on your forehead.

209
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:24,980
If I decide to crush your Stan's
head like the melon it is,

210
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:28,382
then I'm guessing your
head will get crushed too.

211
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:32,669
I'm gonna keep a tight
grip on you for now.

212
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:35,192
We're gonna pay my gramps a little visit.

213
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:37,264
I'm sure he'd love to meet you.

214
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:41,500
And I'd like to know
more about Dio myself.

215
00:14:48,920 --> 00:14:50,000
What the hell?

216
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:53,458
Was that green liquid coming
out of his stand's hand?

217
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,904
You should have listened, Jojo.

218
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:58,880
I told you you're gonna
regret this, didn't I?

219
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:03,040
This is the attack of my
stand, Hierophant Green!

220
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:05,060
No weird moves, Kakyoin!

221
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:15,800
Emerald Splash!

222
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:29,520
So, what do you think?

223
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:31,960
Did you like Emerald Splash?

224
00:15:32,180 --> 00:15:37,300
That fluid you saw in Hierophant Green is
actually a surge of destructive energy.

225
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:40,220
It tore straight through
your stand's chest,

226
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:43,600
and your insides have
now been torn to shreds.

227
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:46,680
And as for that doctor over there...

228
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:51,050
Why?

229
00:15:51,820 --> 00:15:55,080
I know I took that stand
out of her. So how?

230
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:56,560
I told you already.

231
00:15:57,060 --> 00:15:58,420
But let me reiterate.

232
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:02,097
I tried to warn you that by
attacking my hierophant green,

233
00:16:02,180 --> 00:16:03,709
it would hurt her as well.

234
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:08,080
My stand can travel farther than
yours, but it dislikes open spaces.

235
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:11,700
Without exception, it prefers
to hide within something.

236
00:16:12,580 --> 00:16:15,580
If you drag it out, it gets angry.

237
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:20,760
That's why, when you ripped it out of
her throat, it hurt her along the way.

238
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:23,557
You're the one who did this to her.

239
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:25,640
This is entirely your fault, Jojo.

240
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:27,500
You must be held responsible.

241
00:16:27,740 --> 00:16:29,037
Look at what you've done!

242
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:32,020
All you had to do was let me kill you,

243
00:16:32,180 --> 00:16:34,945
and the doctor would have
walked away unharmed.

244
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:40,280
And still, you get up.

245
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:42,460
You are so pathetic.

246
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:47,320
You're nothing more than a sandbag,
about to be pummeled by a skilled boxer.

247
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:49,387
Why even bother standing up?

248
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:51,638
I'm just gonna knock you down again.

249
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:59,677
Look no one ever said
Jotaro Kujo was a nice guy

250
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:04,457
I beat the crap out of
people more than I have to.

251
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:09,597
Some are even still in the hospital
I've had idiot teachers who like

252
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:13,777
to talk big so I taught them a lesson
and they never came back to class.

253
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:17,597
If I go to a restaurant the food's bad.

254
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:20,504
and make it a policy to
stiff him with the bill.

255
00:17:21,820 --> 00:17:24,420
But even a bastard like me

256
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:27,840
can spot true evil when he sees it.

257
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:31,597
True evil are those who
use the weak for their own

258
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:34,680
game and crush them underfoot
when they're through.

259
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:38,060
Especially an innocent woman.

260
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:41,980
And that is exactly what
you've done, isn't it?

261
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:46,912
And your stand gets to hide from the
victim, the law, and the consequences.

262
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:51,097
That's why I will judge you myself.

263
00:17:51,180 --> 00:17:53,957
I'm evil. See?

264
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:54,977
That's where you're wrong.

265
00:17:55,060 --> 00:17:57,037
Evil is always the loser.

266
00:17:57,120 --> 00:17:59,117
It's the victor who has justice.

267
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:01,777
The victim being the last man standing.

268
00:18:01,860 --> 00:18:03,817
And how you win in battle?

269
00:18:03,900 --> 00:18:04,880
is irrelevant.

270
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:17,360
See, the loser is always the evil one.

271
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,540
Time to finish you off.

272
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,230
Really?

273
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:23,060
The loser's evil?

274
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:25,010
Emerald

275
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:26,730
Splash!

276
00:18:27,320 --> 00:18:29,100
Then let me show you.

277
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:33,150
What?

278
00:18:33,900 --> 00:18:34,782
There's no way!

279
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,417
No one can just deflect
the Emerald Splash!

280
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:39,620
Just how evil you are!

281
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:59,157
I'll teach you justice...

282
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:00,680
...with my stat!

283
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,280
Your stand has incredible power.

284
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:17,020
You caught me by surprise earlier
and scratched its chest a little.

285
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,520
I'm glad my stand isn't weak,

286
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:23,620
but sometimes it feels like it
can get more savage than I am.

287
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:25,780
That was a close call.

288
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:31,969
She'll be fine once
her wounds are treated.

289
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:34,520
Did a gaspike just burst?

290
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:36,357
He came from the doctor's office!

291
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:37,937
Everyone, stay in the classroom!

292
00:19:38,020 --> 00:19:39,697
I'll leave the cleanup to them.

293
00:19:39,780 --> 00:19:42,015
They've had enough school for one day.

294
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:43,900
This guy needs to talk.

295
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:46,807
I want to hear everything
he knows about Dio.

296
00:20:17,420 --> 00:20:21,067
I just have the most amazing
connection with my son right now.

297
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:24,417
Jotaro must be thinking about
me at school this very second.

298
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:26,088
I'm not thinking about you.

299
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:28,190
Jotaro!

300
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:29,771
Why aren't you at school?

301
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:31,557
And who is that boy on your shoulder?

302
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:33,900
Is that blood that he's covered in?

303
00:20:34,220 --> 00:20:35,140
Wait a sec.

304
00:20:35,820 --> 00:20:37,820
Please don't tell me you did that.

305
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,334
None of your business.

306
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:42,160
I need to find the old man.

307
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:45,937
Finding someone in this
big house really sucks.

308
00:20:46,020 --> 00:20:48,597
I think you can find him
with Abdul right now.

309
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,386
They're both in the tea room.

310
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:54,320
Oh, Jotaro.

311
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:56,460
You never tell me anything.

312
00:20:57,340 --> 00:21:01,400
All that does is make me
worry about you all the time.

313
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:06,417
But still, I know that deep
down you really do mean well.

314
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:09,097
You're a very sweet little boy at heart.

315
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:10,800
Hey? Yes?

316
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:16,280
You're looking a little bit
pale this morning You alright?

317
00:21:20,540 --> 00:21:21,370
Yay!

318
00:21:21,453 --> 00:21:23,280
I'm fine! Thank you!

319
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:27,880
I knew it.

320
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:32,960
Well, I hate to say it, but
But it's too late for him.

321
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:35,346
There's no way he'll make it.

322
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:38,440
He's got a few days
before he dies at most.

323
00:21:39,300 --> 00:21:42,380
Jotaro, this is not your fault. Trust me,

324
00:21:42,660 --> 00:21:44,617
do you want to know why this man swore his

325
00:21:44,700 --> 00:21:47,876
allegiance to Dio and came
to your school to kill you?

326
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:51,160
Look right here, and I will show you!

327
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:55,360
What the hell is that?

328
00:23:29,500 --> 00:23:30,817
This is very bad.

329
00:23:30,900 --> 00:23:32,020
At this rate.

330
00:23:32,260 --> 00:23:34,537
A little cold isn't bad from time to time.

331
00:23:34,620 --> 00:23:36,738
I have no idea why I want to either.

332
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:39,440
This is the one thing I feared the most.

333
00:23:39,660 --> 00:23:41,300
Tell me, what can we do?
